---
export const prerender = true;
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SITE_URL } from '../lib/site';

const updated = '2026-09-01';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service | PCGameFit"
  description="The terms governing use of PCGameFit — what our tools are, how our estimates should be treated, and the limits of our liability."
  jsonLd={{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "WebPage",
    "name": "Terms of Service",
    "url": `${SITE_URL}/terms`,
    "dateModified": updated
  }}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Terms of Service' }]} />

    <header class="page-head">
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="lede">Last updated: 1 September 2026</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>1. Acceptance</h2>
      <p>By using PCGameFit.com you agree to these terms. If you do not agree with them, please do not use the site.</p>

      <h2>2. What this service is</h2>
      <p>PCGameFit provides free, browser-based tools that estimate PC gaming performance: compatibility checks, frame-rate estimates, bottleneck analysis, hardware rankings and power-supply sizing. All tools are provided for informational purposes.</p>

      <h2>3. Accuracy of estimates</h2>
      <p>Our figures are <strong>modelled estimates, not measured benchmark results</strong>. They are derived from published system requirements and aggregated hardware performance data. Real-world performance varies with drivers, operating system, background load, thermals, memory configuration, game patches and individual hardware samples.</p>
      <p>Do not treat our output as a guarantee. In particular, do not make a purchase decision solely on the basis of a number produced by this site — verify against independent reviews and, where possible, retailer return policies.</p>

      <h2>4. Hardware and game data</h2>
      <p>Product names, logos and cover artwork belong to their respective owners. Game artwork is sourced from SteamGridDB and remains the property of the relevant publishers and rights holders. We claim no ownership over third-party trademarks and are not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by any hardware manufacturer, game developer or publisher named on this site.</p>

      <h2>5. Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You may use the site for personal and commercial reference. You may not:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Scrape, mirror or bulk-download the site or its underlying data without written permission</li>
        <li>Attempt to disrupt, overload or gain unauthorised access to the service</li>
        <li>Present our estimates as measured benchmark results, or as your own original data</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. No warranty</h2>
      <p>The service is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including but not limited to warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement.</p>

      <h2>7. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>To the fullest extent permitted by law, PCGameFit is not liable for any indirect, incidental or consequential damages arising from use of the site — including, without limitation, purchasing decisions made in reliance on our estimates.</p>

      <h2>8. External links</h2>
      <p>We link to third-party sites for reference. We do not control those sites and are not responsible for their content, accuracy or privacy practices.</p>

      <h2>9. Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update these terms. Material changes will be reflected in the "last updated" date above. Continued use after a change constitutes acceptance.</p>

      <h2>10. Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about these terms can be sent via our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
